(P/'independent-source-proof-assessment.json').write_text(json.dumps({'subject':root,'scope':'Full current claim and proof check of this targeted mathematical defect source; no unrelated whole audit.', 'confirmed_defect':'Empty cellular basis index sets yield zero cells, while unqualified shared-block iff could treat them as a vacuous path without supported block.','smallest_sound_route':'Retain arbitrary empty sets; define zero-cell support empty/no simple factors, restrict block chain to nonzero cells, leave all original head/purity/corner outputs intact.','complete_proof_check':[{'anchor':'1.1','finding':'Comparing left/right cell products gives the symmetric associative Gram scalar; empty index sets have the unique zero form and no entries to compare.'},{'anchor':'1.2','finding':'Handle zero cell and zero layer first. For nonzero finite cell, equality of left/right central actions on its tensor layer forces scalar action; orthogonal central idempotents select exactly one supported block. No Gram inverse, so nonzero zero-form cells are included.'},{'anchor':'2.1','finding':'A nonzero form coefficient lets cell rank-one operators generate every basis vector from any vector outside the radical. Radical is the unique maximal submodule and quotient absolutely simple under every field extension.'},{'anchor':'3.1','finding':'For an actual simple choose maximal finite cell ideal acting nontrivially; higher ideals annihilate it. A zero-form or zero cell layer cannot act nontrivially, so a nonzero form head is obtained.'},{'anchor':'3.2','finding':'If a cell label fails to dominate another, their common upper ideal shapes lie strictly above the first and act trivially on its cell quotient. Ideal support forces multiplicity order, diagonal multiplicity one and distinct simple labels.'},{'anchor':'4.1','finding':'Absolute simple heads make the finite algebra split. Primitive-idempotent projection is exact; symmetric associative head pairing makes involution preserve head labels, giving equal left/right factor multiplicities. Cell-layer dimension additivity proves the corner identity; zero layers add zero.'},{'anchor':'5.1','finding':'Nonzero corners give the primitive graph, with repeated equivalent idempotents linked via semisimple matrix units. Nonnegative corner sum identifies each edge with a shared simple factor of an actual nonzero cell. Every nonzero finite cell has a simple factor, and head exhaustion realizes all simple vertices. Hence nonzero-cell chains exactly recover blocks. A zero cell has no vertex or edge and empty block support.'},{'anchor':'6.1','finding':'All rich original nonzero head, exhaustion, purity, ordering, corner and chain outputs retained over arbitrary fields; zero index sets now covered explicitly. Zero algebra has no simple/head/block selections and all relevant sums are vacuous.'}], 'choice':'Only finite module/basis/index operations are used in this local verification; no new source-reading or arbitrary-choice claim is invented.','mathematical_round':1,'maximum_rounds':2,'original_repair_history':'Prior unrelated B repairs/counters unchanged.'},indent=2)+'\n');print('6direct46total focused consumer checks sealed')
